{"aliases":[],"authority_links":[{"id":"A001342","kind":"dila_authority","label":"DILA 人名規範","url":"https://authority.dila.edu.tw/person/search.php?aid=A001342"}],"bio_en":"Śubhakarasiṃha (637–735) was an Indian monk who arrived in Chang'an in 716. Working with the Chinese monk Yixing, he translated the Mahāvairocana Sūtra and explained its ritual and contemplative practices. Yixing recorded his explanations in a commentary that became central to East Asian esoteric Buddhism. The teachings associated with this scripture underlie the Womb Realm tradition. He is remembered with Vajrabodhi and Amoghavajra as one of the Three Great Masters of the Kaiyuan era.","bio_summary":"開元三大士之一，傳胎藏密法，譯《大日經》。","chronology":[],"dates":"637-735","doctrine_nodes":["胎藏界","大日經"],"dynasty":"唐","lineages":[{"certainty":"traditional","display_note":"密教邊作 traditional/譯場脈絡顯示，仍須與經錄互證。","edge_id":"mi--subhakarasimha--yixing","evidence_refs":[{"claim":"一行承善無畏胎藏法脈。","claim_scope":"traditional","note":"密教邊作 traditional/譯場脈絡顯示，仍須與經錄互證。","ref":"CBETA T50n2061_002","source_id":"song-gaoseng-zhuan"},{"claim":"一行承善無畏胎藏法脈。","claim_scope":"traditional","note":"密教邊作 traditional/譯場脈絡顯示，仍須與經錄互證。","ref":"CBETA T55n2154_009","source_id":"kaiyuan-shijiao-lu"},{"claim":"一行承善無畏胎藏法脈。","claim_scope":"traditional","note":"密教邊作 traditional/譯場脈絡顯示，仍須與經錄互證。","ref":"T50n2061/T55n2154","source_id":"cbeta-online"}],"from_master_id":"subhakarasimha","lineage_id":"mi","note":"一行承善無畏胎藏法脈。","relation_type":"teacher","source_ref":"CBETA T50n2061_002、T55n2154_009","source_work":"宋高僧傳／開元釋教錄","to_master_id":"yixing"}],"master_id":"subhakarasimha","name":"善無畏","name_en":"Shanwuwei (Śubhakarasiṃha)","name_full":"善無畏三藏","portrait":{"attribution":"Anonymous, via Wikimedia Commons","caption":"善無畏三藏傳像","confidence":"traditional_portrait_medium","image_url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/40/%C5%9Aubhakarasi%E1%B9%83ha_14th_century%2C_Kamakura%2C_National_Museum%2CTokyo.jpg","license":"Public domain","original_thumbna